terms.medium_def:
David's compatriot living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.2.18; 
only referred to as Asahel (עֲשָׂהאֵל); 
his mother was Zeruiah; 
a brother of Abishai and Joab; 
father of Zebadiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.21.1; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
father of Zephaniah.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.21; 
only referred to as Jaasiel (יַעֲשִׂיאֵל); 
a son of Abner.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1Ch.9.12; 
referred to as Maasai (מַעֲשַׂי), or Amashsai (KJV= Amashai) (עֲמַשְׁסַי); 
a son of Adiel. § a priest who returned from exile

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.23.1; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
a son of Adaiah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.28.7; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
son of Ahaz; 
a brother of Hezekiah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.23; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
a son of Ananiah; 
father of Azariah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.5; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
a son of Baruch.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.7; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
a son of Ithiel; 
father of Kolaiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Jer.29.21; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
father of Zedekiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Jer.35.4; 
only referred to as Maaseiah (מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ); 
a son of Shallum.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Ezr.10.15; 
only referred to as Asahel (עֲשָׂהאֵל); 
father of Jonathan.

A man from the tribe of Simeon(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.35; 
only referred to as Asiel (עֲשִׂיאֵל); 
father of Seraiah. § a Simeonite and ancestor of Jehu

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.30; 
only referred to as Asaiah (עֲשָׂיָה); 
a son of Haggiah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.37; 
only referred to as Ephlal (אֶפְלָל); 
a son of Zabad; 
father of Obed. § a descendant of Pharez

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.25; 
only referred to as Palal (פָּלָל); 
a son of Uzai. § son of Uzai and one who assisted in restoring the walls of Jerusalem in the time of Nehemiah

A priest living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.12; 
only referred to as Pelaliah (פְּלַלְיָה); 
a son of Amzi; 
father of Jeroham. § son of Amzi and ancestor of Adaiah the priest in the time of Nehemiah

A location in Edom first mentioned at Gen.36.35; 
referred to as Midian or Midianite (מִדְיָן), or Midianite woman (מִדְיָנִי), or Midianite (מְדָנִי), or Midian (Μαδιάν). § the tribe descended from Midian
inhabitant of the territory of the tribe descended from Midian; located principally in the desert north of the Arabian peninsula; land to which Moses went when he fled from Pharaoh

Jacob's daughter living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.30.21; 
only referred to as Dinah (דִּינָה); 
daughter of Israel and Leah; 
a sister of Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar and Zebulun; 
half-sister of: Dan, Naphtali, Gad, Asher, Joseph and Benjamin. § daughter of Jacob by Leah, full sister of Simeon and Levi

Jacob's son who founded the tribe of Dan living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.30.6; 
only referred to as Dan (דָּן); 
son of Israel and Bilhah; 
a brother of Naphtali; 
half-brother of: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Gad, Asher, Issachar, Zebulun, Dinah, Joseph and Benjamin; 
father of Hushim.

A location in Dan Tribe first mentioned at Gen.14.14; 
referred to as Dan or Danite (דָּן), or Dan or Danite (דָּנִי), or Laish (לַ֫יִשׁ), or Leshem (לֶ֫שֶׁם). § ♣1) descendants of Dan, son of Jacob
2) inhabitants of the territory of Dan

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.2; 
only referred to as Midian (מִדְיָן); 
son of Abraham and Keturah; 
half-brother of: Ishmael and Isaac; 
a brother of Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Ishbak and Shuah; 
father of Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida and Eldaah.

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.2; 
only referred to as Medan (מְדָן); 
son of Abraham and Keturah; 
half-brother of: Ishmael and Isaac; 
a brother of Zimran, Jokshan, Midian, Ishbak and Shuah. § a son of Abraham by Keturah

David's son from the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.3.3; 
referred to as Chileab (כִּלְאָב), or Daniel (דָּנִיֵּאל, דָּנִאֵל); 
a son of David and Abigail; 
half-brother of: Amnon, Absalom, Adonijah, Shephatiah, Ithream, Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon, Ibhar, Elishua, Nepheg, Japhia, Elishama, Eliada, Eliphelet, Tamar, Elpelet, Nogah and Jerimoth.

A man of the Gomerians living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.10.3; 
referred to as Riphath (רִיפַת), or Riphath (דִּיפַת); 
son of Gomer; 
a brother of Ashkenaz and Togarmah. § the 2nd son of Gomer

A man of the Gomerians living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.10.3; 
referred to as Riphath (רִיפַת), or Riphath (דִּיפַת); 
son of Gomer; 
a brother of Ashkenaz and Togarmah. § the 2nd son of Gomer

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.26; 
referred to as Israel or [ ] or Israelite or "God" (KJV= Israel) (יִשְׂרָאֵל), or Israel (Aramiac יִשְׂרָאֵל), or Jacob or "he" (KJV= Jacob) (יַעֲקֹב), or Jeshurun (יְשֻׁרוּן), or Israelite (יִשְׂרְאֵלִי), or Israelitess (יִשְׂרְאֵלִית), or Israel or Israelite (Ἰσραήλ), or Jacob (Ἰακώβ), or Israelite or Israel (Ἰσραηλίτης); 
son of Isaac and Rebekah; 
a brother of Esau; 
husband of Rachel, Leah, Zilpah and Bilhah; 
father of Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Dan, Naphtali, Gad, Asher, Issachar, Zebulun, Dinah, Joseph and Benjamin. § a symbolic name for Israel describing her ideal character

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1Ch.2.18; 
only referred to as Jesher (יֶ֫שֶׁר); 
son of Caleb and Azubah(?); 
a brother of Hur, Shobab, Ardon, Mesha, Haran, Moza, Gazez, Sheber, Tirhanah, Regem(?), Jotham(?), Geshan(?), Pelet(?), Ephah(?), Shaaph(?), Shaaph, Sheva and Achsah. § one of the sons of Caleb and grandson of Hezron by wife Azubah

A location first mentioned at 1Ch.27.29; 
referred to as Sharon (שָׁרוֹן), or Sharonite (שָׁרוֹנִי), or Sharon (KJV= Saron) (Σάρων). § Sharonite, of Sharon "a plain"
inhabitant of the district of Sharon

A king of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.24.17; 
referred to as Zedekiah (צִדְקִיָּ֫הוּ), or Mattaniah (מַתַּנְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Josiah and Hamutal; 
a brother of Jehoahaz; 
half-brother of: Jehoiakim and Shallum.

A High Priest from the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.8.17; 
only referred to as Zadok (צָדוֹק); 
a son of Ahitub; 
father of Ahimaaz.

A High Priest from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.12; 
only referred to as Zadok (צָדוֹק); 
a son of Ahitub; 
father of Shallum.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.22.11; 
only referred to as Zedekiah (צִדְקִיָּ֫הוּ); 
a son of Chenaanah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.15.33; 
only referred to as Zadok (צָדוֹק); 
father of Jerusha.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Jer.29.21; 
only referred to as Zedekiah (צִדְקִיָּ֫הוּ); 
a son of Maaseiah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.4; 
only referred to as Zadok (צָדוֹק); 
a son of Baana.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.29; 
only referred to as Zadok (צָדוֹק); 
a son of Immer.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.16; 
only referred to as Zedekiah (צִדְקִיָּ֫הוּ); 
son of Jehoiachin; 
a brother of Shealtiel.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Jer.36.12; 
only referred to as Zedekiah (צִדְקִיָּ֫הוּ); 
a son of Hananiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.19.16; 
only referred to as Shaphat (שָׁפָט); 
father of Elisha.

David's son from the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.3.4; 
only referred to as Shephatiah (שְׁפַטְיָהוּ); 
a son of David and Abital; 
half-brother of: Amnon, Chileab, Absalom, Adonijah, Ithream, Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon, Ibhar, Elishua, Nepheg, Japhia, Elishama, Eliada, Eliphelet, Tamar, Elpelet, Nogah and Jerimoth.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.13.5; 
only referred to as Shaphat (שָׁפָט); 
a son of Hori.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.22; 
only referred to as Shaphat (שָׁפָט); 
son of Shemaiah; 
a brother of Hattush, Igal, Bariah and Neariah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.29; 
only referred to as Shaphat (שָׁפָט); 
a son of Adlai.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at 1Ch.9.8; 
only referred to as Shephatiah (שְׁפַטְיָהוּ); 
a son of Reuel; 
father of Meshullam.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.16; 
only referred to as Shephatiah (שְׁפַטְיָהוּ); 
a son of Maacah.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.21.2; 
only referred to as Shephatiah (שְׁפַטְיָהוּ); 
son of Jehoshaphat; 
a brother of Jehoram, Azariah, Jehiel, Zechariah, Azariahu and Michael.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.4; 
only referred to as Shephatiah (שְׁפַטְיָהוּ); 
a son of Mahalalel; 
father of Amariah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Jer.38.1; 
only referred to as Shephatiah (שְׁפַטְיָהוּ); 
a son of Mattan.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.34.24; 
only referred to as Shiphtan (שִׁפְטָן); 
father of Kemuel. § an Ephraimite, father of Kemuel, the leader of the tribe selected to divide the promised land between the tribes
